<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB sells no wheat in 17th tender.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB sells no wheat in 17th tender.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said there were no successful bids in the latest national pool tender. The total amount bid for was 16,000 tonnes, it said.</p>
<p>The two highest failed bids were for Australian Standard White in Newcastle at A$171.50 a tonne and for feed wheat in Newcastle at A$161.50 a tonne.</p>
<p>Closing date for the next tender is March 5.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 973-1800</p>
